From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:31:29 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] prefs: Default check-alive-timeout to 20 seconds

A window that does not answer a ping within check-alive-timeout gets the
"not responding" dialog (Wait / Force Quit). At 5 seconds it pops up
over games and apps that block their main thread while compiling
shaders or loading a level, and the user has to dismiss it every time.

Raise the default to 20000 ms. The key keeps working as before: any
value in milliseconds, and 0 disables the check and the dialog.
---
 data/org.gnome.mutter.gschema.xml.in | 8 +++++---
 src/core/prefs.c                     | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/data/org.gnome.mutter.gschema.xml.in b/data/org.gnome.mutter.gschema.xml.in
index 2b97f94..cbde4d2 100644
--- a/data/org.gnome.mutter.gschema.xml.in
+++ b/data/org.gnome.mutter.gschema.xml.in
@@ -125,12 +125,14 @@
     </key>
 
     <key name="check-alive-timeout" type="u">
-      <default>5000</default>
+      <default>20000</default>
       <summary>Timeout for check-alive ping</summary>
       <description>
         Number of milliseconds a client has to respond to a ping request in
-        order to not be detected as frozen. Using 0 will disable the alive check
-        completely.
+        order to not be detected as frozen. When it expires the "not
+        responding" dialog (Wait / Force Quit) is shown. Using 0 will disable
+        the alive check and the dialog completely. The default is long enough
+        for shader compilation and game loading screens.
       </description>
     </key>
 
diff --git a/src/core/prefs.c b/src/core/prefs.c
index 163402d..0ba3705 100644
--- a/src/core/prefs.c
+++ b/src/core/prefs.c
@@ -99,7 +99,7 @@ static gboolean bell_is_audible = TRUE;
 static gboolean gnome_accessibility = FALSE;
 static gboolean gnome_animations = TRUE;
 static gboolean locate_pointer_is_enabled = FALSE;
-static unsigned int check_alive_timeout = 5000;
+static unsigned int check_alive_timeout = 20000;
 static char *cursor_theme = NULL;
 /* cursor_size will, when running as an X11 compositing window manager, be the
  * actual cursor size, multiplied with the global window scaling factor. On
